  "exact_results": [
    "For j<=r, the real ratio r!/(r-j)! equals the natural descending factorial cast to real. The denominator is proved nonzero.",
    "For rho>=0 and j<=r<ell, (rho/ell)^j r!/(r-j)! <= rho^j. Nat.descFactorial_le_pow and r<=ell supply the bound.",
    "For 0<=rho<=1 and j<=r<ell, the same ratio is at most 1. Taking j=r gives (rho/ell)^r r!<=1.",
    "For 0<rho<=1 and positive natural ell, 0<rho/ell<=1. The nonnegative-scale lemma also holds at ell=0 under Lean real division."
  ],
  "boundary_cases": "The main loss and source theorems require r<ell, hence ell is positive. j=0, r=0 and rho=0 are included using ordinary natural-power conventions. No subtraction underflow occurs in the factorial ratio because j<=r.",
